WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.540
Since construction of the International Space
Station started to wrap up in the late 2000s,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.360
NASA has had the idea to construct an ISS
for the moon.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.060
Over the years, NASA has received support
from multiple presidents for the Lunar Gateway

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.350
and they have sunk billions into the project.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.910
But, just last year, NASA announced that the
Lunar Gateway was no longer a critical path

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.010
to the moon.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:27.330
So, why is the Lunar Gateway failing to take
shape.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.500
Well, taking a look at the origins of the
Lunar Gateway, we’ll find ourselves in April

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.170
of 2010.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:39.609
At the time, President Obama called for NASA
to complete a crewed mission to a nearby asteroid.

00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:43.960
Nasa would quickly determine that such a mission
would be infeasible.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.719
Astronauts would have to spend months in a
spacecraft and the technology simply wasn’t

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:48.719
ready yet.

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:53.940
So, Nasa would reject this plan, but ironically,
they would propose an alternate plan that

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.409
was arguably even crazier.

00:00:56.409 --> 00:00:59.609
This alternate plan was the asteroid redirect
mission.

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:04.489
The idea was that a spacecraft could go and
grab a small near earth asteroid and take

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:06.650
it into orbit around the moon.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:11.079
This way, astronauts could go and live in
the spacecraft attached to the asteroid and

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:13.659
explore the asteroid over a long period of
time.

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:16.090
Congress wasn’t a big fan of the idea though.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.210
They didn’t believe that the mission was
either practical or useful.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:25.170
This rejection would lead us into 2017 where
NASA revealed their vision for the modern

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.490
lunar gateway.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.619
Nasa proposed a two phase plan with the first
phase calling for the assembly of a collection

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:35.340
of space modules in a distant orbit around
the moon called the deep space gateway.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.399
They originally planned for this phase to
be completed by the late 2020s at which point

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.100
they could move onto phase 2 which was the
deep space transport.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.039
The deep space transport was simply a large
spacecraft that could shuttle astronauts from

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.990
the moon to mars.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:52.689
Nasa hoped that assembling this spacecraft
at the deep space gateway would reduce the

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:56.439
difficulty of launching such a large spacecraft
directly from earth.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:00.909
This plan wouldn’t quite pan out either,
but it would take on a new form.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:05.200
You see, President Trump would call on Nasa
to not only send astronauts to the moon, but

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.060
also build a new permanent presence in space.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.580
The guidelines for Nasa weren’t too strict,
so Nasa would build upon their past lunar

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.500
space station ideas and propose the most ambitious
version of the Gateway.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.860
This version involved help from many of the
space leaders around the world including Russia,

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.790
Japan, Europe, and Canada.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.240
The gateway was proposed to have 9 different
modules including a habitation module, a robotic

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:32.210
arm, a docking component, and a plethora of
science modules.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.290
At this point, Nasa was basically just pitching
the idea of building an ISS around the moon.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:42.050
Though extremely ambitious, Nasa was able
to garner support from several space leaders,

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.840
so it seemed like the Lunar Gateway would
actually take shape.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.040
But this is when Vice President Pence would
completely redirect the focus of Nasa in March

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.330
of 2019.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.390
Pence wouldn’t cancel the Lunar Gateway,
but he would put out a goal that would require

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.610
basically all of Nasa’s focus.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.090
Pence wanted Nasa to return astronauts to
the moon in 2024.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.650
Given this new goal, Nasa would be forced
to completely change around their priorities

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.980
and timelines.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.750
They would cancel or postpone everything that
wasn’t required to return humans to the

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:10.870
moon.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.810
And unfortunately, the majority of the Lunar
Gateway was not required to return people

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.200
to the moon.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.040
But this brings up the question.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.070
If the Lunar Gateway is not required to return
people to the moon, why was Nasa spending

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:25.540
so much money and effort on the project in
the first place?

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.200
Given that we haven’t been able to return
humans to the moon in nearly 50 years, you

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.860
would think that getting to the moon would
be a top priority and that all distractions

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.520
would already be cut out.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.980
Well, the answer to this question is extremely
complicated as there are several experts on

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.290
both sides of the argument.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.560
Some think that the Lunar Gateway is a no
brainer for long term human spaceflight while

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.220
others suggest that the Lunar Gateway is an
utter waste of time, money, and effort.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:55.150
So, let’s begin by taking a look at the
proponents of the Lunar Gateway starting with

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.980
Nasa themselves.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:01.210
Nasa claims that there are three primary reasons
to support the development of Gateway with

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:03.870
the first being the power and propulsion element.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:08.290
The Lunar Gateway is expected to support a
60 kilowatt solar electric propulsion system,

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.740
top of the line communications systems, attitude
control, and orbital transfer capabilities.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.410
Nasa argues that positioning all of this tech
near the astronauts visiting the moon will

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.790
highly improve the likelihood of a successful
mission.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.500
For instance, even if the astronauts were
not able to communicate with mission control

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.080
on earth, they may be able to contact the
Lunar Gateway.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.600
Similarly, if something goes wrong with their
rocket, they may be able to stay on the self-sustaining

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.250
Lunar Gateway.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.290
Basically, astronauts traveling to the moon
will have more options available if a major

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.970
error occurs with the mission.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:44.270
Nasa’s second argument in favor of the Lunar
gateway is the gateway’s ability to act

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:46.410
as a habitation and logistics output.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:50.870
Till now, we have only completed a couple
of manned missions to the moon and all of

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.490
them were rather short.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:57.940
Apollo 11, for instance, only included 21
hours and 36 minutes on the lunar surface.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.320
The short mission durations can be explained
by the fact that there was no long term living

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.800
facility located right next to the moon.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.110
Astronauts in the Apollo missions had a limited
amount of food and resources, so they couldn’t

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.470
just spend 6 months at the moon.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:14.820
The Lunar Gateway, however, would make this
possible.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.310
Astronauts could live inside the Lunar Gateway
for several months at a time and complete

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.420
dozens of trips to the moon.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:24.480
Along with this, we have Nasa’s third reason
for supporting the Lunar Gateway which is

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.410
its logistical capabilities.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:31.270
The Gateway would be much larger than nearly
all modern rockets, so Nasa can use the Gateway

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.750
for storage and transportation purposes.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:37.670
Before each lunar mission, Nasa can send a
wide variety of different experiments and

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.100
testing equipment to the lunar gateway.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.210
And during the mission, the astronauts would
be able to bring back lunar samples and conduct

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.160
various tests on them at the gateway itself.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.420
The ability to conduct tests near the moon
would allow Nasa to conduct many more tests

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.320
and be much more flexible.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.380
After all, to get more lunar samples, you
don’t have to launch another rocket to the

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.380
moon.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.530
You just have to descend to the Lunar surface
and collect some more samples.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:07.140
That’s the main reasons that Nasa offers
on their official page about the Lunar Gateway.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.840
But there is one more advantage that proponents
of the gateway often point to which is a transition

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.000
point for a martian mission.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.300
Getting to mars takes about 6 months with
today’s technology, so a large spacecraft

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:23.210
with nice sleeping, bathroom, and exercising
facilities would be optimal.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.650
Launching such a spacecraft directly from
earth would be extremely difficult due to

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.790
the large size of the spacecraft.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:33.740
But what if we launched components of a large
spacecraft into space piece by piece and assembled

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.080
it in space like the Deep Space Transport
plan suggested.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.430
The hardest part of launching a large spacecraft
is getting it into space.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.340
Once the spacecraft is in space, it’s much
easier to move it around due to a lack of

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.160
gravity, air resistance, and drag.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.580
By following this plan, astronauts could simply
fly in a regular cramped rocket to the lunar

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.580
gateway.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:57.340
And at the Lunar Gateway, they could transition
into the large spacecraft to complete their

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.210
journey to Mars.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:02.420
This would heavily reduce the pressure of
trying to build a massive rocket that can

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.669
fly directly from Earth to Mars.

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:07.980
Not to mention, this would give the astronauts
a much more comfortable way to travel.

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:11.790
So, that’s the points that proponents of
the gateway bring up.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.960
Now, let’s take a look at the other side.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.360
Some notable critics include former nasa administrator
Michael Griffin and the founder of the Mars

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.100
Society Robert Zubrin.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:26.090
These critics argue that the Lunar Gateway
is not only a money pit, but completely pointless.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:30.130
Like most space projects, the Lunar Gateway
is expected to cost a lot of money coming

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.570
in at $40 billion.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:36.710
And let’s not forget that space projects
tend to often overrun their budgets by quite

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.710
a bit.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:43.520
So, it would not be surprising to see the
gateway end up costing $60 or even $70 billion.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.620
Something else to consider is that going to
the gateway to get to the moon adds 17% to

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:49.820
the fuel cost of getting to the moon.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.620
Aside from costing a massive amount of money,
building the gateway would likely take several

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:54.620
years.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:59.479
It took 10 years to build the ISS itself and
that’s only in low earth orbit.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:02.979
Imagine how long it could take to build a
space station in lunar orbit.

00:08:02.979 --> 00:08:06.870
The worst part though is that all of that
money and effort doesn’t even give us any

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.110
new capabilities.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:12.740
Sure, having a lunar gateway would be convenient
for conducting experiments with lunar samples.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:17.320
But, it’s not like those same experiments
can’t just be completed on earth or at the

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.590
ISS.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.460
What about astronaut safety though?

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:24.020
Building a lunar gateway can significantly
improve the safety of astronauts visiting

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.020
the moon.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:30.430
Well, the primary argument against this point
is that we can just build a lunar base instead.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:35.110
Why spend all that money and effort on building
a lunar ISS when you could just spend all

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.889
that money and effort on building a lunar
base.

00:08:37.889 --> 00:08:41.329
A lunar base would accomplish all of the functions
of a Lunar Gateway better.

00:08:41.329 --> 00:08:46.459
If you’re going to argue that the gateway
is convenient, well the base is even more

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:47.459
convenient.

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:50.000
You can live and conduct experiments right
on the moon.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.619
If you’re going to argue that the gateway
provides greater safety, well the base provides

00:08:54.619 --> 00:08:56.180
even more safety.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.180
With a base, you don’t even have to ascend
to the gateway to return to safety or contact

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.790
mission control.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:05.730
Most importantly though, building a lunar
base would be a major step forward in terms

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.079
of space exploration.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:11.260
We’ve already built a massive space station,
so building one for the moon would be more

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.980
of a sideways step.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.550
Building a lunar base though would give us
valuable experience that could help us eventually

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:19.450
build a base and city on Mars.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.600
Basically, people who are against the gateway
argue that a lunar base and the gateway offer

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.899
very similar pros and cons.

00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:30.910
So, why not just go ahead and take the bigger
leap forward and build a base instead of jacking

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:33.029
around with another space station.

00:09:33.029 --> 00:09:37.800
As for what Nasa plans to do, though the gateway
has been postponed, they haven’t completely

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.520
ditched it quite yet.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.540
But given the strong opposition from credible
experts, it’s very possible that the ISS

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:46.240
for the moon will never end up happening.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.740
That’s not necessarily a bad thing though.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:52.449
It just means we have more money and resources
to build a lunar base instead.

00:09:52.449 --> 00:09:54.990
Do you guys support the lunar gateway?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.110
Comment that down below.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.959
Also, drop a like if you guys are excited
to finally see humans return to the moon.

00:10:00.959 --> 00:10:04.800
And of course, consider joining our discord
community to suggest future video ideas and

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.389
consider subscribing to see more questions
